Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["How wide is the critical region?",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The Ginzburg number is 7.6 to 11.4, far above 1. The condition ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
     SubsuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["SF",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], 
      StyleBox["red",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "\[GreaterGreater]", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["Gi",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c654bbf7-1ebf-44c4-a4ba-9c2578eeb067"],
 " of mean-field theory therefore holds at no temperature where the form of \
Ginzburg and Landau applies: even at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
     SubsuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["SF",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], 
      StyleBox["red",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "\[LongEqual]", "1"}],
    TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "03b405ec-2777-4d2c-85f1-92718011528c"],
 " the Gaussian fluctuations alone give ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["C", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["fl",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], "/", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["C", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["Gi",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       StyleBox["SF",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       StyleBox["X", "TI"]], ")"}], 
     RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]], "\[TildeTilde]", "3"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9c60ccb4-bf42-404f-bd5e-d356f1ccdd4c"],
 ". The width ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["Gi",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["c",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "21cfe454-b7ca-4adf-8314-2061746c89fe"],
 " is larger than the critical temperature itself and of the order of the \
cutoff. The reason is in the table: the correlation length ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[Xi]", 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["GL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "945513a2-1b00-48d3-87a2-e3feb907ca1c"],
 " is about ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"1", "/", 
    SubscriptBox["\[CapitalLambda]", 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "171d8757-f43e-4fb5-99c6-f0e60365bfe7"],
 ", the shortest length of the model, because the pairs are tightly bound \
(there is no Fermi surface, and the pairing needs a coupling above the \
critical one), and the specific-heat jump per correlation volume is about \
0.04, far below 1: a correlation volume holds much less than one degree of \
freedom, while mean-field theory needs many. (In a superconductor of Bardeen, \
Cooper and Schrieffer the correlation length is large against the distance of \
the electrons and the Ginzburg number, of the order of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["c",
        FontSlant->"Plain"]], "/", 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["E", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["F",
        FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], ")"}], "4"], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "780f4497-bb6d-490d-a332-4c07f403eab9"],
 " with the Fermi energy ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["E", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["F",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c5e66a95-ae9d-44d3-9cc5-5d14d1714b00"],
 ", is tiny; here the opposite holds.) The error of the regularization does \
not change the conclusion (the last column). ",
 StyleBox["What this means for Section III.T (a remark, and why it matters).",
  
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The statements of Section III.T.6 are statements about the mean-field free \
energy, and as such they are correct and checked. But the temperatures at \
which that free energy shows the behaviour of Landau's theory, from about ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["0.4", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "542cca9c-21bf-4e35-a382-e35b9f099732"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["0.98", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9fd1c9bd-771d-4835-8c0b-05b6649cc7dc"],
 " of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["c",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b494dd8b-90b3-444e-bbe7-ea1b06039033"],
 ", lie inside the critical region. The mean-field theory of the five methods \
therefore does not describe the superfluid near its transition: the critical \
temperatures, the exponent ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   FractionBox["1", "2"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "861b6e92-e820-4baf-962e-f15f5f2188ac"],
 " of the order parameter and the continuity of the transition are not \
reliable. It matters because the five methods agree with each other there, \
and agreement among mean-field methods is no evidence when all of them omit \
the same fluctuations. A reliable description of the transition needs a \
calculation beyond the methods: for example the three-dimensional theory of a \
complex isospin vector with two quartic invariants and with the gauge fields \
on a lattice (the method used for the thermal transition of the electroweak \
theory by K. Kajantie, M. Laine, K. Rummukainen and M. Shaposhnikov, 1996), \
or the Gaussian fluctuations of the auxiliary pair field in HS (the method of \
P. Nozieres and S. Schmitt-Rink, 1985, for pairs bound more tightly than \
their distance)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ff7fe135-a01c-420d-a75c-4c0120a52e43"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
III.G.8 Can the superfluid play the role of the Higgs particle, and is the \
Higgs a composite particle?\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"5104524f-c0a3-4f25-9b3a-c0870419c883"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Two questions.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Whether the superfluid can play the role of the Higgs particle has two \
meanings. (b) Can it be the Higgs field of the Standard Model? No, in every \
method, and the answer needs no number: the only matter field of the model is \
the DiracLike spinor, which has electric charge 0 and no quantum numbers of \
the electroweak group ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["SU", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", "2", ")"}], 
     StyleBox["L", "TI"]], "\[Times]", 
    StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", "1", ")"}], 
     StyleBox["Y", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b5e9be53-7fc4-4e6e-b871-3456df4c5aeb"],
 ", so every field made of it, the condensate included, is a singlet of the \
electroweak group. Its vacuum value leaves that group unbroken and gives no \
mass to the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["W", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "561a6794-a9e7-467f-9c6f-bcec82882026"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "58f245d1-8f88-4c25-9eca-ac2bb70ff0c9"],
 " bosons of nature, and its amplitude mode has no coupling at tree level to \
them, to the quarks or to the leptons, the couplings by which the Higgs boson \
of nature is identified. The model contains no coupling between the two \
sectors; a term such as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
       StyleBox["SM",
        FontSlant->"Plain"]], ")"}], "\[Dagger]"], 
    SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
     StyleBox["SM",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], "\[Dagger]"], "\[CenterDot]", 
    OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9499b745-5bd3-42e5-b01b-78af3189bad7"],
 " would be an addition to the model, would mix the amplitude mode with the \
Higgs boson of nature, and would be limited by the measured couplings of that \
boson. (The first version of this section compared the superfluid with the \
Higgs boson of the Standard Model as if the two gauge groups were one; that \
comparison had no basis and is withdrawn.) (a) Is the superfluid the Higgs \
field of its own gauge group ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["SU", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", "2", ")"}], 
     StyleBox["v",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[Times]", 
    StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", "1", ")"}], 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["F",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8b2b2564-5c7c-4c62-84dc-dc2f3b2838e3"],
 ", with a Higgs particle? The rest of this section answers (a) with the \
quantities of the new group alone; its scale is not known, and every mass is \
in units of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalLambda]", 
    StyleBox["LL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a0ca4eac-3dc6-470b-aba3-63b95bbfe897"],
 ". ",
 StyleBox["The scale of the breaking.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["W", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["SF",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["g", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["v",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["I",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8cb3c60b-fd81-4a98-a6b9-62df0558b646"],
 " with the isospin decay constant ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["I",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"2", 
       SubsuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["SF",
         FontSlant->"Plain"], 
        StyleBox["X", "TI"]]}], ")"}], 
     RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]], 
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", 
      StyleBox["SF",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0e203d6b-b292-4d79-a2c6-f09304628529"],
 ", where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1f164685-c42d-4ede-b030-0be2717936e2"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f92fc5ed-b5ca-4264-9f2b-6d49be8444ae"],
 " are the coefficients of the two invariants of the kinetic part of the \
field, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
      RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", 
       OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"]}], 
      "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "2"], "+", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox[
        OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], "\[Dagger]"], "\[CenterDot]",
        "\[PartialD]", 
       OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"]}], 
      "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "2"], "/", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
      OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], 
      "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "2"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "993907cf-70a6-487e-b8df-e701c5cf7c44"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
    RowBox[{"0", ",", 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "37675b33-4244-4e27-bf9d-6b8fb5d0e9ca"],
 " is the field of the vacuum at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "33d1a993-0f7d-4c23-b459-97f8bcda700d"],
 "; the decay constant of the phase is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["F",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"2", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         SubsuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["SF",
           FontSlant->"Plain"], 
          StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "+", 
         SubsuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["SF",
           FontSlant->"Plain"], 
          StyleBox["X", "TI"]]}], ")"}]}], ")"}], 
     RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]], 
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", 
      StyleBox["SF",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "eb6b0641-3809-4db6-842a-1c747ad8da1a"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["Z", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["SF",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", "2", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["g", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["F",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["F",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "36fa06e2-9f18-4e9a-af36-37c55f6e634d"],
 ". With the convention ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["W", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    StyleBox["gv", "TI"], "/", "2"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c1d00124-711f-4a07-9925-8dfbd04f3ef0"],
 " by which the Standard Model defines its vacuum value, the scale of the \
breaking and the quartic coupling are"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7f063d64-08ef-42e3-aebe-755de75af15d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["v", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", "2", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["I",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], ",", "      ", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["W", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["g", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["LL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["v",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["v", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], ",", "      ", 
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[Lambda]", 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["H",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], "\[LongEqual]", 
   FractionBox[
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["SF",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
        StyleBox["H",
         FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], ")"}], "2"], 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"(", 
       SubsuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["v", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["SF",
         FontSlant->"Plain"], 
        StyleBox["X", "TI"]], ")"}], "2"]}]], ","}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 FontFamily->"Times",
 FontSize->1.25 
  Inherited,ExpressionUUID->"d68f610c-d005-449b-a854-f8d185f26646"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "with the mass ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["H",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f3dab48c-b85e-46bd-8a5a-b6fe48c46813"],
 " of the amplitude (Higgs) mode and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["NU",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a5832961-e073-4b17-8154-8bce8de6ecca"],
 " of the non-unitary doublet from the linear response of Part II (the exact \
small oscillations of each method). ",
 StyleBox["The width of the amplitude mode.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " On the field ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", 
        StyleBox["SF",
         FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
       StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "+", 
      StyleBox["h", "TI"], "/", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"2", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{
           SubsuperscriptBox[
            StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
            StyleBox["SF",
             FontSlant->"Plain"], 
            StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "+", 
           SubsuperscriptBox[
            StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
            StyleBox["SF",
             FontSlant->"Plain"], 
            StyleBox["X", "TI"]]}], ")"}]}], ")"}], 
       RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]]}], ")"}], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
      SubscriptBox["\[CurlyTheta]", "0"]}]], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["e", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], "3"]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e27d0e16-ded9-4951-959c-824171c3f61a"],
 " (the amplitude field ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["h", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f1fc86a5-ea2c-4fc4-a350-8a08977ad4a2"],
 " normalized canonically and the phase ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[CurlyTheta]", "0"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "92069cf7-df11-47cf-8f86-6cfa24627001"],
 "), and on the same field rotated about ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], "1"], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b61797af-45bf-4c6c-9a63-d2fcf2978c04"],
 " by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[CurlyTheta]", "1"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bd5dbec7-fdac-40ef-aa7c-f95a27a1c0f9"],
 ", the kinetic part contains the couplings ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["F",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["h", "TI"], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", 
       SubscriptBox["\[CurlyTheta]", "0"]}], ")"}], "2"]}], TraditionalForm]],
   "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6dce4a87-cf7f-48b3-93ce-ac0ec6e9a8cb"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox[
       RowBox[{"(", 
        SubsuperscriptBox[
         StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["SF",
          FontSlant->"Plain"], 
         RowBox[{
          StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
          StyleBox["I",
           FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], ")"}], "2"], "/", 
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["SF",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
        StyleBox["F",
         FontSlant->"Plain"]}]]}], ")"}], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["h", "TI"], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", 
       SubscriptBox["\[CurlyTheta]", "1"]}], ")"}], "2"]}], TraditionalForm]],
   "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "013717c7-61e9-499c-96bc-042ce803ba13"],
 " (and the same for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[CurlyTheta]", "2"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "39386062-adc6-48e1-9e5a-572344a9a065"],
 "). With the canonical Goldstone fields ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["F",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], 
    SubscriptBox["\[CurlyTheta]", "0"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c092afb8-ac02-44f2-895d-d549a1e3eaf9"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["I",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], 
    SubscriptBox["\[CurlyTheta]", 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e6fafb23-5dec-438b-b808-9c2ee883bab2"],
 " all three couplings are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"1", "/", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["F",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b4d2c78a-569d-45cf-85d0-46e3e670ff53"],
 "; the decay of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["h", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "be798961-c08b-4e29-9ea8-cdda5f0141b7"],
 " at rest into two massless quanta of one canonical field has the amplitude ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["SF",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
        StyleBox["H",
         FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], ")"}], "2"], "/", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["F",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e37df6e0-1642-4638-9ee5-623cb15886e2"],
 " and the width ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["SF",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
        StyleBox["H",
         FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], ")"}], "3"], "/", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"32", "\[Pi]", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       RowBox[{"(", 
        SubsuperscriptBox[
         StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["SF",
          FontSlant->"Plain"], 
         RowBox[{
          StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
          StyleBox["F",
           FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], ")"}], "2"]}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c8b33970-8040-476b-b02b-0abd7667dd7e"],
 " (the phase space of two identical massless particles), and the three \
channels give"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"73231154-7e18-4a9c-91f8-562be83b409d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["H",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], "\[LongEqual]", 
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{"3", "\[ThinSpace]", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"(", 
       SubsuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["SF",
         FontSlant->"Plain"], 
        RowBox[{
         StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
         StyleBox["H",
          FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], ")"}], "3"]}], 
    RowBox[{"32", "\[Pi]", "\[ThinSpace]", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"(", 
       SubsuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["SF",
         FontSlant->"Plain"], 
        RowBox[{
         StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
         StyleBox["F",
          FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], ")"}], "2"]}]], "."}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 FontFamily->"Times",
 FontSize->1.25 
  Inherited,ExpressionUUID->"98f964ca-e79e-4006-b29d-edd5197dbbf8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "With the gauge fields the Goldstone fields are the longitudinal parts of \
the massive gauge bosons (the equivalence theorem of J. M. Cornwall, D. N. \
Levin and G. Tiktopoulos 1974 and of M. S. Chanowitz and M. K. Gaillard \
1985), so that the same formula gives the width into ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["W", "TI"], "+"], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["W", "TI"], "-"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "03c4e34c-24fa-4e06-8c6f-75a2204234c9"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["ZZ", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f95444a1-56f4-4619-b03e-1b81f37f8549"],
 " of the new group, up to corrections that the cells after the table of the \
Higgs sector compute. With ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["F",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9f757c9b-5de1-4131-9afa-1471ba7d55e1"],
 " replaced by the vacuum value ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["v", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a3ca7f41-73e2-4440-93cc-00043aed1ba6"],
 " of the Standard Model, the same formula is the known width ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"3", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["m", "TI"], "3"], "/", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"32", "\[Pi]", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["v", "TI"], "2"]}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "15505097-80ef-42ab-9a64-62fbd5cb0f87"],
 " of a heavy Higgs boson of mass ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ea00ed35-367f-4cb6-9985-2d1d2903d7cc"],
 " into its longitudinal ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["W", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "79905458-df75-4a35-9b5b-9635ffac6481"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "546e7316-eafb-4d43-8161-8a7ed342c0df"],
 " bosons, a check of the normalization. ",
 StyleBox["A remark on the width (what it means and why it matters).",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The formula uses the effective Lagrangian at the energy ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["H",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "41607886-5584-47f3-ab81-831496316e5c"],
 ", where it is not accurate (its mass of the amplitude mode differs from the \
linear response by 7.0 to 17 per cent, as the cell after the table of the \
Higgs sector computes), so it estimates the order of magnitude only. It \
matters because the conclusion drawn from it, that the amplitude mode is a \
broad resonance and not a narrow particle, needs only the order of magnitude: \
the width is 2 to 4 times the mass. The next cell derives the two couplings \
by exact differentiation of the kinetic part (symbolic, with real symbols), \
and compares them with the closed forms and the Rust values."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4f54161b-a8a4-4041-8ea9-d5e02152426e"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
    "the", " ", "couplings", " ", "of", " ", "the", " ", "amplitude", " ", 
     "field", " ", "to", " ", "the", " ", "Goldstone", " ", "fields", " ", 
     "by", " ", "exact", " ", "differentiation", " ", "of", " ", "the", " ", 
     "kinetic", " ", "part", " ", "along", " ", "a", " ", "line", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"gzX", ":", " ", 
      RowBox[{"the", " ", "field", " ", "at", " ", "gzX", " ", "is", " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"gzP0", " ", "+", " ", 
         RowBox[{"gzAmp", "/", "gzNh"}]}], ")"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"e", "^", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"i", " ", "gzD0", " ", "gzX"}], ")"}]}], " ", "R_", "1", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"gzD1", " ", "gzX"}], ")"}], " ", "e_", "3", " ", "with", " ",
        "the", " ", "constant", " ", "amplitude", " ", "gzAmp", " ", "and", " ",
        "the", "\n", "   ", "gradients", " ", "gzD0"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"gzD1", " ", "of", " ", "the", " ", "two", " ", "angles", " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"R_", "1"}], ":", " ", 
        RowBox[{"the", " ", "rotation", " ", "about", " ", "e_", "1"}]}], 
       ")"}]}], ";", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"gzKin", " ", "is", " ", "Z"}], " ", "|", "dPhi", "|", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"^", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", "Y"}], " ", "|", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Phi", "^", "dag"}], " ", "dPhi"}], "|", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"^", "2"}], "/"}], "|", "Phi", "|", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"^", "2"}], "\n", "   ", "at", " ", "gzX"}]}], " ", "=", " ", 
      
      RowBox[{
      "0", " ", "with", " ", "the", " ", "coefficients", " ", "gzZz"}]}]}], ",",
     " ", 
    RowBox[{"gzYy", " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"all", " ", "symbols", " ", "real"}], ")"}]}]}], " ", "*)"}], 
  "\n", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"gzField", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"gzP0", " ", "+", " ", 
        RowBox[{"gzAmp", "/", "gzNh"}]}], ")"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
       RowBox[{"I", " ", "gzD0", " ", "gzX"}], "]"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"-", 
         RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
          RowBox[{"gzD1", " ", "gzX"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
         RowBox[{"gzD1", " ", "gzX"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"gzKin", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"ph", " ", "=", " ", 
          RowBox[{"gzField", " ", "/.", " ", 
           RowBox[{"gzX", " ", "->", " ", "0"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"dph", " ", "=", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"D", "[", 
            RowBox[{"gzField", ",", " ", "gzX"}], "]"}], " ", "/.", " ", 
           RowBox[{"gzX", " ", "->", " ", "0"}]}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
       "   ", 
       RowBox[{"ComplexExpand", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"gzZz", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "dph", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", "dph"}]}], 
         " ", "+", " ", 
         RowBox[{"gzYy", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "ph", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", "dph"}], 
             "]"}], "^", "2"}], "/", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "ph", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", "ph"}], 
            ")"}]}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
   RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"the", " ", "coefficients", " ", "of", " ", "gzAmp", " ", 
        RowBox[{"gzD0", "^", "2"}], " ", "and", " ", "of", " ", "gzAmp", " ", 
        
        RowBox[{"gzD1", "^", "2"}]}], ":", " ", 
       RowBox[{
       "the", " ", "derivative", " ", "in", " ", "gzAmp", " ", "at", " ", 
        "gzAmp"}]}], " ", "=", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
      "with", " ", "the", " ", "canonical", "\n", "   ", "normalization", " ",
        "gzNh"}], " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"2", " ", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"Z", " ", "+", " ", "Y"}], ")"}]}], ")"}], "^", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}], ")"}]}], " ", "of", " ", "the", " ", 
       "amplitude", " ", "field"}]}]}], " ", "*)"}], "\n", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"gzCouplings", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Coefficient", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"D", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"gzKin", " ", "/.", " ", 
                RowBox[{"gzD1", " ", "->", " ", "0"}]}], ",", " ", "gzAmp"}], 
              "]"}], " ", "/.", " ", 
             RowBox[{"gzAmp", " ", "->", " ", "0"}]}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"gzD0", "^", "2"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Coefficient", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"D", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"gzKin", " ", "/.", " ", 
                RowBox[{"gzD0", " ", "->", " ", "0"}]}], ",", " ", "gzAmp"}], 
              "]"}], " ", "/.", " ", 
             RowBox[{"gzAmp", " ", "->", " ", "0"}]}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"gzD1", "^", "2"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], " ", "/.", " ", 
        RowBox[{"gzNh", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
          RowBox[{"2", " ", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"gzZz", " ", "+", " ", "gzYy"}], ")"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ",", 
       "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"gzZz", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"gzZz", " ", "+", " ", "gzYy"}], " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",",
           " ", 
          RowBox[{"gzP0", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Print", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<the couplings of h to (d theta_0)^2 and (d theta_1)^2: \>\"",
       ",", " ", "gzCouplings", ",", 
      " ", "\"\< = {f_F, f_I^2/f_F} with f_F = (2 (Z + Y))^(1/2) Phi0, f_I = \
(2 Z)^(1/2) Phi0\>\""}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Do", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"z", " ", "=", " ", 
           RowBox[{"rustPart3", "[", 
            RowBox[{"\"\<p3_Z_\>\"", " ", "<>", " ", "t"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"y", " ", "=", " ", 
           RowBox[{"rustPart3", "[", 
            RowBox[{"\"\<p3_Y_\>\"", " ", "<>", " ", "t"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"p0", " ", "=", " ", 
           RowBox[{"rustPart3", "[", 
            RowBox[{"\"\<p3_Phi0_\>\"", " ", "<>", " ", "t"}], "]"}]}], ",", 
          " ", "g", ",", " ", "fF", ",", " ", "fI"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"g", " ", "=", " ", 
          RowBox[{"gzCouplings", " ", "/.", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"gzZz", " ", "->", " ", "z"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"gzYy", " ", "->", " ", "y"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"gzP0", " ", "->", " ", "p0"}]}], "}"}]}]}], ";", "\n", 
         "   ", 
         RowBox[{"fF", " ", "=", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
            RowBox[{"2", " ", 
             RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{"z", " ", "+", " ", "y"}], ")"}]}], "]"}], " ", 
           "p0"}]}], ";", " ", 
         RowBox[{"fI", " ", "=", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
            RowBox[{"2", " ", "z"}], "]"}], " ", "p0"}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
         RowBox[{"check", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"\"\<WP3-H2 \>\"", " ", "<>", " ", "t"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"thName", "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "<>", 
            " ", "\"\<: the couplings of h to (d theta_0)^2 and (d theta_1)^2 \
by exact differentiation of the kinetic part, \>\"", " ", "<>", " ", 
            RowBox[{"ToString", "[", 
             RowBox[{"NumberForm", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"g", "[", 
                RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "8"}], "]"}], "]"}],
             " ", "<>", " ", "\"\< and \>\"", " ", "<>", " ", 
            RowBox[{"ToString", "[", 
             RowBox[{"NumberForm", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"g", "[", 
                RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "8"}], "]"}], "]"}],
             " ", "<>", 
            " ", "\"\<, = f_F and f_I^2/f_F and = Rust (largest relative \
difference)\>\""}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
           RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"g", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], "/", "fF"}], " ", "-", " ", 
               "1"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"g", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], "/", 
                RowBox[{"(", 
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{"fI", "^", "2"}], "/", "fF"}], ")"}]}], " ", "-", 
               " ", "1"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"g", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], "/", 
                RowBox[{"hgRust", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "\"\<fF\>\""}], "]"}]}], " ", "-", 
               " ", "1"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"g", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], "/", 
                RowBox[{"(", 
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{
                   RowBox[{"hgRust", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "\"\<fI\>\""}], "]"}], "^", "2"}], 
                  "/", 
                  RowBox[{"hgRust", "[", 
                   RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "\"\<fF\>\""}], "]"}]}], ")"}]}], 
               " ", "-", " ", "1"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"10", "^", 
            RowBox[{"-", "10"}]}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"\"\<P3-H2 \>\"", " ", "<>", " ", "t"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"\"\<YP3-H2 \>\"", " ", "<>", " ", "t"}]}], "]"}]}]}], 
       "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "thTags"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ";"}]}]}]], "Input",\

