Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The answer to question (a) for each method",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", judged by the properties that make a field the Higgs field of a gauge \
group and its amplitude mode a Higgs particle."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9940aec2-e2a4-4f93-b74d-6bf23284ca49"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The Higgs mechanism.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " In every method the condensate gives the masses ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["W", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["SF",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["g", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["v",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["I",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bc43a4fa-decb-4473-ba90-23f54ec1a0a5"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["Z", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["SF",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", "2", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["g", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["F",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["F",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "76ea21fe-fe78-42fa-af41-097716c9edff"],
 " to the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], "\[PlusMinus]"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4d58fcaa-5e31-4556-b3a6-e5903086ff34"],
 " and the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d41711d7-bb21-4531-9f8d-5943db0fbaf1"],
 " of the superfluid, leaves exactly one gauge boson, the zeugon ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], "3"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7858291f-5aca-4b05-beeb-b3b80ffcd4ae"],
 " (not the photon), massless, and turns the three Goldstone fields into the \
longitudinal parts of the massive bosons: the superfluid does for the new \
group what a Higgs field does."
}], "ItemNumbered",ExpressionUUID->"673390f5-bdd6-4e3b-bd02-12ecd7098148"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["A scalar of charge 0 below the threshold.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " In every method the amplitude mode (charge ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["Q", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "17181e4b-0ae1-4bdd-b222-b6efc7a5d9c9"],
 ") lies below the threshold of two quasi-particles, at 0.82 to 0.90 of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"2", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["E", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["gap",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "df6bc683-04b2-4360-b4cf-92ca21ccd91a"],
 ": a bound state of the mean-field dynamics."
}], "ItemNumbered",ExpressionUUID->"65d3bffd-a24c-411b-a1ef-f49ffab31a23"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Its mass against the scale of the breaking.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["H",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], "/", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["v", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "faa081a7-f3a0-4326-a9df-644fd11e3dcb"],
 " is 4.46 to 5.69 and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[Lambda]", 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["H",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "58a1d161-76e6-4f24-b6ec-6b29f67d0895"],
 " is 9.9 to 16.2: the amplitude mode is heavier than the scale of the \
breaking. Whether a quartic coupling of this size is compatible with the \
perturbative unitarity of the scattering of the longitudinal gauge bosons of \
this group is not decided here: the bound depends on the scalar fields and \
the channels of the theory, and it was not computed for this one."
}], "ItemNumbered",ExpressionUUID->"42e12120-8602-4c39-8d3c-347e5da8eedb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Its width.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["H",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], "/", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["H",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "09acf95d-ebe9-408d-80dd-511050aca4e5"],
 " is 2.1 to 3.9: once the decays into Goldstone fields are allowed, the \
width exceeds the mass, and the amplitude mode is a broad resonance, not a \
particle."
}], "ItemNumbered",ExpressionUUID->"92838989-c0a0-432b-95f3-cbd4bc94ae41"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Further scalars.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Every method has the non-unitary doublet, two scalars of the charges ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["Q", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{"\[PlusMinus]", "1"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bb111a13-838d-4cdb-a166-5032a65bfaef"],
 " at 0.99 to 1.09 times ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["H",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5f7d8188-5b1c-4b9d-bbcd-79c4d9254ff5"],
 "."
}], "ItemNumbered",ExpressionUUID->"4d9e4bea-69ee-41da-b28b-59f886702ae6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The quantum numbers.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The condensate is an isospin vector of fermion number 2 of the vector-like \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["SU", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", "2", ")"}], 
     StyleBox["v",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "82fdd60f-8aca-4166-8f51-3f0ae28c376d"],
 ", a group of the DiracLike spinor that is not part of the electroweak \
theory. The zeugon is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], "3"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6689e25f-7a4f-4f6f-8c86-1f19feb67a07"],
 " (no mixing angle), the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "de4e55d0-e16c-42e9-a384-8d2f0b551eb9"],
 " is the gauge boson of the fermion number, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["W", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["SF",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "/", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["Z", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["SF",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "077d14bf-63e3-4757-8207-e89c48ea4b7b"],
 " depends on two independent couplings. The mass of the DiracLike spinor \
does not come from the condensate as a Yukawa mass: the condensate adds a \
pairing gap to a Dirac mass that the vector-like theory allows without it."
}], "ItemNumbered",ExpressionUUID->"5888c8f5-a703-422b-9c88-fa46bbad1467"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The thermal history.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The transition of the superfluid lies deep in its own critical region \
(Section III.G.7); its mean-field temperature, 1.6 to 1.8 times ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["v", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "10cc7905-7524-44a6-96a0-a8a77b0c3d16"],
 ", is not reliable."
}], "ItemNumbered",ExpressionUUID->"50ea6a9a-5a3c-4f2b-aa53-df1a06ec48a1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The verdict.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " (a) In every method the superfluid is the Higgs field of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["SU", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", "2", ")"}], 
     StyleBox["v",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[Times]", 
    StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", "1", ")"}], 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["F",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d3942fc2-b55e-4af2-8935-60964fb3d4e8"],
 ": it breaks the group to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", "1", ")"}], 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["Q",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0e7d3f45-b733-48f1-91f8-ce946f9fc622"],
 ", gives masses to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], "\[PlusMinus]"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "945955a1-ba53-40ad-be9c-a668eae63df4"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4176501e-5fd8-4c09-9769-bcc81990f3dc"],
 ", leaves the massless zeugon, and has a Higgs-like scalar of charge 0 below \
the threshold of two quasi-particles. That scalar is a Higgs particle only in \
the mean-field dynamics: once it can decay into the longitudinal gauge bosons \
it is a resonance broader than its mass, accompanied by the two non-unitary \
scalars of the charges ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[PlusMinus]", "1"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2427d14f-6833-4fd0-bb22-55140d05a074"],
 " of about the same mass. The methods differ in degree, not in kind: CJT and \
KS have the lightest and narrowest amplitude mode, HS ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", "1"}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "234e7f68-1502-4086-8125-9e08c43e55e2"],
 " the heaviest and broadest. (b) In no method is the superfluid the Higgs \
field of the Standard Model, for the reason of structure stated at the \
beginning of this section. ",
 StyleBox["Is the Higgs a composite particle?",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " In this model, yes, in every method, for the Higgs particle of the new \
group: the field ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "83d88582-c495-46ae-a632-2dfd84034e69"],
 " is not a field of the Lagrangian, whose only matter field is the DiracLike \
spinor. It is the amplitude of the pair self-energy, a composite of two \
spinor charges; its kinetic part has no term of its own and is generated \
entirely by the spinor field (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "458ab523-f997-4b00-a506-ac0887e6651a"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "98dbd5b1-871a-445f-bcfe-2fa78ed33f53"],
 " are susceptibilities of the spinor field); and its amplitude mode is a \
bound state of two quasi-particles below their threshold. This is the \
compositeness condition of W. A. Bardeen, C. T. Hill and M. Lindner (1990): \
the normalization of the composite field vanishes at the cutoff, where only \
the spinor field exists. The same structure explains why the composite is \
heavy against the scale of the breaking: in the dynamics of Y. Nambu and G. \
Jona-Lasinio (1961) the mass of the bound state is tied to the gap of the \
spinor charges, while the scale of the breaking comes from a loop of the \
spinor field and is small against the gap. A light composite needs a large \
ratio of the cutoff to the gap, or a different mechanism, for example a \
scalar that is itself a pseudo-Goldstone boson of a larger broken symmetry \
(D. B. Kaplan and H. Georgi 1984). Whether the Higgs boson of nature is \
composite is not decided here, because the Higgs particle of this model is \
not that boson (answer (b)); the measured couplings of the Higgs boson of \
nature agree with those of an elementary Higgs field at the level of several \
per cent, which constrains, but does not exclude, its compositeness at a \
higher scale."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"68f94538-5586-479b-8c51-184ca09a6cbe"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Part R. The revised hypotheses: the superfluid as the Higgs field of the \
Standard Model\
\>", "Chapter",ExpressionUUID->"8751d4eb-8033-47ef-8a10-5a97084be6d8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "On 21 November 2026, at 17:09 PST, the author asked to modify the \
hypotheses so that the superfluid can be the Higgs field of the Standard \
Model, with the same quantum numbers as the Higgs doublet; at 19:38 PST he \
added a second singlet field of hypercharge ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"-", 
    FractionBox["3", "4"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5cbe94b2-f8ce-4786-91bc-6a2f542ca00d"],
 ". Parts I to III of this notebook state the earlier hypotheses, under which \
the spinor field carries no electroweak quantum numbers. This part states the \
revised hypotheses and repeats, in the Wolfram Language and in exact \
arithmetic wherever that is possible, the checks of the four stages of the \
revision that were computed by Rust programs: the quantum numbers of the \
fields and of their pairs (Section R.1, program ",
 StyleBox["sh_quantum",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 "), the ground state of the superfluid (R.2, ",
 StyleBox["sh_superfluid",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 "), the masses of the gauge bosons and the modes of the superfluid (R.3, ",
 StyleBox["sh_higgs",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 ") and the dynamics in time (R.4, ",
 StyleBox["sh_dynamics",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 "). The five remarks made during the revision, R8 to R12, are stated where \
they belong, each with the computation on which it rests, what it means and \
why it matters."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bf0fd2d1-d694-4bc9-96af-9747ef1b5bf3"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
R.0 The fields, the interaction, and how the checks of this part are named\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"9f99cc05-45f8-4708-9ed6-e6c5221e7e1a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The fields.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " In the second version of the revised hypotheses, the current one, there \
are three Dirac fields, all singlets of colour and all of the mass ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", "0.2"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c570de39-b873-4468-b28c-cc92ce4cdc46"],
 " in units of the momentum cutoff ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[CapitalLambda]", 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", "1"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2ffda4fe-2913-4bd2-9b4d-c8aef9e84dbe"],
 ": the isodoublet ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalPsi]", 
    StyleBox["LL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "860abc0c-3d85-4b83-8ae5-dbe7bc0d80d2"],
 ", an up and a down component, each a Dirac spinor of four components, with \
the hypercharge ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SM",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    FractionBox["1", "4"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3c4ccd0e-f3f7-47c6-b636-cb2c711637ac"],
 "; the singlet ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[Chi]", 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a8954609-e422-43b1-9188-deccf0431812"],
 ", with the hypercharge ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   FractionBox["1", "4"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3cf9bea1-241d-449a-9de3-bbac9ae98d42"],
 "; and the singlet ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[Chi]", 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[Prime]"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d5134848-2f24-46d7-b7bb-fb7fe75aa42f"],
 ", with the hypercharge ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"-", 
    FractionBox["3", "4"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "cc5cc148-78aa-41ab-9ff4-c33b270982b7"],
 ". The electric charges ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["Q", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SM",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"3", ",", 
      StyleBox["SM",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], "+", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SM",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e66f4aaf-9854-4ec8-b2b9-2d8dc08da3e1"],
 ", with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["SM",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6c8663c3-41e3-4b35-8603-8783521b1e32"],
 " (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", "1", ",", "2", ",", "3"}], 
   TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1e1e9b77-1e57-4e4f-91f6-679c1fc7354f"],
 ") the generators of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["SU", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", "2", ")"}], 
     StyleBox["L", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "654fabe8-49cc-4b0d-a2e6-32ca23510637"],
 ", are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   FractionBox["3", "4"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "47b15d5a-ce8b-4baa-a59c-f0b6eaafc423"],
 " (up), ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"-", 
    FractionBox["1", "4"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8d1c22b5-cf48-43bd-af2f-a0a2418453f5"],
 " (down), ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   FractionBox["1", "4"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4ff9a6da-3126-4842-bd31-049f762205ba"],
 " (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[Chi]", 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4533467c-0131-463f-9d5a-d5b4a065f2ed"],
 ") and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"-", 
    FractionBox["3", "4"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8be9fbfe-cc04-4446-ada7-425fa9027879"],
 " (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[Chi]", 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[Prime]"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f4660a8a-8f83-4549-9128-71ec7338a91e"],
 "); antiparticles carry the opposite charges. The first version of the \
revised hypotheses, which this part keeps as the comparison, had no ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[Chi]", 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[Prime]"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "82c40533-5cdb-4b5e-b149-18d14c28e02c"],
 ". The code numbers the sixteen components of the field ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[CapitalPsi]", 
      StyleBox["LL",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]], ",", 
     SubscriptBox["\[Chi]", 
      StyleBox["SH",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]], ",", 
     SubsuperscriptBox["\[Chi]", 
      StyleBox["SH",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[Prime]"]}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "83f6cac4-fb42-4573-955b-25a5ec5decc3"],
 " from 0: the components ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"0", ",", "\[Ellipsis]", ",", "7"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ce31e157-3059-48e9-92f3-9307a705a0a5"],
 " belong to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalPsi]", 
    StyleBox["LL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "63f19b87-172c-4a1a-adaf-eb26be6cc109"],
 " (the component ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"2", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], "+", 
    StyleBox["s", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "dec30d04-658c-473a-8b6e-746894ebbbad"],
 " has the Dirac index ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", "0", ",", "\[Ellipsis]", ",", "3"}], 
   TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c295a551-5cdd-4d8e-b82e-9776fa4d2398"],
 " and the isospin index ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["s", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4ee99244-00dd-4d6f-a024-152169a267b3"],
 ", 0 for up and 1 for down), ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"8", ",", "\[Ellipsis]", ",", "11"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b9a56f91-691d-48a0-8745-e2b21aae4d0e"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[Chi]", 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d1afb981-0c38-43ee-87af-c088628f9cb7"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"12", ",", "\[Ellipsis]", ",", "15"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3681060b-1d7e-4822-9a2e-4b6e6649f9b8"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[Chi]", 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[Prime]"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b44f5d97-b4a1-4ea0-9d2a-00474d604887"],
 ". The Dirac matrices are those of the chiral basis, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[Gamma]", 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "0"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{"(", "\[NoBreak]", GridBox[{
       {"0", 
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["1",
          FontFamily->"Helvetica",
          FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"]},
       {
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["1",
          FontFamily->"Helvetica",
          FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "0"}
      },
      GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Center}}, "Rows" -> {{Baseline}}},
      GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {
          Offset[0.27999999999999997`], {
           Offset[0.7]}, 
          Offset[0.27999999999999997`]}, "Rows" -> {
          Offset[0.2], {
           Offset[0.4]}, 
          Offset[0.2]}}], "\[NoBreak]", ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "014f6e4e-b94d-49dd-9a91-c29514194257"],
 ", with the chirality ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[Gamma]", 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["ch",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[Gamma]", 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "0"], 
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[Gamma]", 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "1"], 
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[Gamma]", 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], 
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[Gamma]", 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "3"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    StyleBox["diag",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", "1", ",", "1"}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "31615387-191e-4a9e-8f13-d438d466bdf5"],
 " and the charge-conjugation matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["C", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[Gamma]", 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], 
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[Gamma]", 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "0"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "db306d4c-49b7-4df6-9a2b-1bcc6f8dc6a9"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"19180745-42d7-43e4-9397-82b272d588a6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The symmetries.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Besides the gauge group ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["SU", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", "2", ")"}], 
     StyleBox["L", "TI"]], "\[Times]", 
    StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", "1", ")"}], 
     StyleBox["Y", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "58a88139-58e9-4829-8252-732d97850983"],
 ", the free fields have the global groups generated by the particle number \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["F", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["tot",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "54f1b585-af2d-4970-9635-6f92216d17c0"],
 " (one for every particle of the three fields), by the relative number ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["R", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "62ae7813-4536-4d5a-9e91-91733d72effc"],
 " (the number of particles of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalPsi]", 
    StyleBox["LL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1a3645c8-3b03-4b56-9e62-69bbe0601532"],
 " minus that of the two singlets) and by the generators ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["R",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2f1c61ea-042f-4bd0-93cb-b62cf9caed0e"],
 " of the custodial group ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["SU", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", "2", ")"}], 
     StyleBox["R",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b8a70c99-a135-48a9-9893-2b016e9d96c1"],
 ", which rotates the pair ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[Chi]", 
      StyleBox["SH",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]], ",", 
     SubsuperscriptBox["\[Chi]", 
      StyleBox["SH",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[Prime]"]}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a4937597-441b-476e-b31e-1fead5bed591"],
 " as a doublet. The hypercharge is the combination"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a4c1b49c-d6de-4677-a087-6f76f21f30d9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SM",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{"3", ",", 
     StyleBox["R",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], "+", 
   FractionBox["1", "4"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["R", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], ",", "      ", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Q", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SM",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"3", ",", 
     StyleBox["SM",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], "+", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{"3", ",", 
     StyleBox["R",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], "+", 
   FractionBox["1", "4"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["R", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], "."}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 FontFamily->"Times",
 FontSize->1.25 
  Inherited,ExpressionUUID->"a1785ee4-454b-450e-bf33-d7e3b8d5a412"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The interaction.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The Hamiltonian density contains the free Dirac terms of the three fields, \
the scalar and the vector contact terms of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalPsi]", 
    StyleBox["LL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c32641a7-8844-43ac-b927-66db5ed80019"],
 " of Parts II and III, with the couplings ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["G", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["S",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{"-", "8"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8787e34b-9b0a-42fb-a57d-ea6f280b5598"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["G", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["V",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", "0.8"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a6a163fb-7b85-4d8c-96dd-126b6431c6c6"],
 ", and the pairing terms"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"51d49b5b-4dfb-4f3e-b3af-cfcb527eb944"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"-", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["G", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SH",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["s", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", 
     StyleBox["u",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], ",", 
     StyleBox["d",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}],
    LimitsPositioning->True], 
   RowBox[{"[", 
    RowBox[{":", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"(", 
       SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPi]", 
        StyleBox["SH",
         FontSlant->"Plain"], 
        StyleBox["s", "TI"]], ")"}], "\[Dagger]"], 
     SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPi]", 
      StyleBox["SH",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], 
      StyleBox["s", "TI"]], ":", "+", ":", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"(", 
       SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPi]", 
        StyleBox["SH",
         FontSlant->"Plain"], 
        RowBox[{"\[Prime]", 
         StyleBox["s", "TI"]}]], ")"}], "\[Dagger]"], 
     SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPi]", 
      StyleBox["SH",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], 
      RowBox[{"\[Prime]", 
       StyleBox["s", "TI"]}]], ":"}], "]"}], ","}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 FontFamily->"Times",
 FontSize->1.25 
  Inherited,ExpressionUUID->"04fa689b-95fd-46e8-9f26-d16998032ace"],

Cell["with the pair operators", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"eff62177-55d5-429a-b1ca-93d480958cf2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPi]", 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["s", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPsi]", 
    StyleBox["LL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]], 
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["C", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["LL",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
     SubsuperscriptBox["\[Gamma]", 
      StyleBox["LL",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], 
      StyleBox["ch",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[CircleTimes]", 
     SubsuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["e",
       FontWeight->"Bold",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], 
      StyleBox["SH",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], 
      StyleBox["s", "TI"]]}], ")"}], 
   SubscriptBox["\[Chi]", 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], ",", "      ", 
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPi]", 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{"\[Prime]", 
     StyleBox["s", "TI"]}]], "\[LongEqual]", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPsi]", 
    StyleBox["LL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]], 
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["C", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["LL",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
     SubsuperscriptBox["\[Gamma]", 
      StyleBox["LL",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], 
      StyleBox["ch",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[CircleTimes]", 
     SubsuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["e",
       FontWeight->"Bold",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], 
      StyleBox["SH",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], 
      StyleBox["s", "TI"]]}], ")"}], 
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[Chi]", 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[Prime]"], ","}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 FontFamily->"Times",
 FontSize->1.25 
  Inherited,ExpressionUUID->"428a2d3a-4ede-49dc-b114-99ec8ec74771"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["G", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SH",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", "100.8"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "480f4d89-1506-4059-9452-34b3a9b809f6"],
 ", the isospin columns ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e",
      FontWeight->"Bold",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["SH",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["u",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", "0"}], ")"}], 
     StyleBox["T", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "da1450bd-9975-4c81-861c-c723dd8a5fa1"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e",
      FontWeight->"Bold",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["SH",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["d",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", "1"}], ")"}], 
     StyleBox["T", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b6ba8e9a-b897-4469-8507-9a47a88b0059"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{":", " ", ":"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "aea7002e-dde4-416b-b862-fee30295b28a"],
 " the normal ordering with respect to the normal vacuum. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPi]", 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["s", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "48ee4e41-4698-4c00-93d2-b4e2d5a80a0e"],
 " annihilates a particle of the component ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["s", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f076dd89-6b2f-428f-a882-17886717d3fc"],
 " of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalPsi]", 
    StyleBox["LL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "de2d5110-4137-4863-8da1-346296c3b8a8"],
 " together with a particle of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[Chi]", 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a1951a29-d5e2-46bf-81f8-88de3a8e9bb1"],
 " in the state of spin zero and positive parity, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPi]", 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{"\[Prime]", 
     StyleBox["s", "TI"]}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "aef460f9-80ab-4d24-9736-a45a378e038d"],
 " does the same with a particle of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[Chi]", 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[Prime]"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d5e53a38-89fe-4894-b27a-a3314408dc1e"],
 ". The expectation values ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
     StyleBox["SH",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
       StyleBox["SH",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       StyleBox["u",
        FontSlant->"Plain"]], ",", 
      SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
       StyleBox["SH",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       StyleBox["d",
        FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "97f0b178-1b7f-461a-9324-0ed83c0865a9"],
 " of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPi]", 
      StyleBox["SH",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], 
      StyleBox["u",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]], ",", 
     SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPi]", 
      StyleBox["SH",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], 
      StyleBox["d",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7f77bd38-b30c-4387-be33-6b3d43fc71ce"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[Prime]"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e151963d-3d69-4b2f-b05a-f738bfb25090"],
 " of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPi]", 
      StyleBox["SH",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], 
      RowBox[{"\[Prime]", 
       StyleBox["u",
        FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], ",", 
     SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPi]", 
      StyleBox["SH",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], 
      RowBox[{"\[Prime]", 
       StyleBox["d",
        FontSlant->"Plain"]}]]}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "90d74f84-2558-4890-84cd-bc231f129205"],
 " are the two pair fields, and the superfluid is their condensate. The \
ground state is computed by the five mean-field methods of Part II: HS (1, \
1), HS (0, 1) and HS (0, 0) (the method of Hubbard and Stratonovich with \
three parameter sets), KS (Kohn and Sham) and CJT (Cornwall, Jackiw and \
Tomboulis)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"99c728f4-88af-4010-a499-f301f9ede344"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["How the checks of this part are named.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Each check of this part is one of the checks of the four Wolfram scripts \
of the revision, ",
 StyleBox["wolfram/source/sh_quantum.wls",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["sh_superfluid.wls",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["sh_higgs.wls",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["sh_dynamics.wls",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 ", under the same identifier: W, the letters of the stage (QN, SF, H, D) and \
a number. The scripts were run on the author's computer, and their reports \
are kept with the data of the Rust programs; this part repeats their code \
with the explanations a reader needs. The checks of the three programs of a \
stage do not correspond one to one: one exact check of the Wolfram Language \
often derives what several Rust checks test in floating point, and a few \
checks have no counterpart. Every check therefore names, after its result, \
the checks of the Rust program and of the Python program that test the same \
statements, or \"none\". In stage 2 the identifiers follow the families of \
the Rust checks (WQN-4 tests statements of QN-4a to QN-4c); in the other \
stages they are numbered in the order of the scripts (decision D34 of the \
task record)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"62685ba3-9502-4be1-b554-6605d2bfa4b0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["A clean slate.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The next cell clears every symbol that Parts I to III left in the global \
context of the kernel, except the functions of the register of the checks \
(Chapter 0) and the tools of this part that it defines. The code below uses \
short names for the objects of the algebra (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8ab765de-e8a4-45a9-9935-9be6785c5caf"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["b", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4e56ccfe-0e35-4612-a077-bd1b925290ac"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["g", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "409f8a9d-b07d-4369-87ca-9179fd48d227"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5ea04ca5-8312-4478-bdbe-71d9cf32c0a6"],
 ", ...), many of them as symbols without values; the clean slate makes sure \
that none of them carries a value from an earlier part. This part therefore \
needs only the cells of Chapter 0 before it. Each of the Sections R.2 to R.4 \
starts again from a clean slate, as each of the four scripts runs in a kernel \
of its own."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c1209659-9491-4173-be78-0b8cff0f1db1"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
