Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
R.3.5 Remark R11: in the pairing-only methods the amplitude mode lies exactly \
at the pair self-energy (check WH-5)\
\>", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"5feadccd-a7cf-41fd-92bc-7d80840de4c6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The remark.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " In HS (0, 1) and HS (0, 0) the amplitude mode lies exactly at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[Omega]", 
     StyleBox["SH",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["H",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SH",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "0"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "960a9c29-9ac9-4235-ab4e-9d128f09a177"],
 ", below the threshold of two quasi-particles. ",
 StyleBox["Why it holds.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The response of the pair amplitudes along the amplitude and along the \
phase of the vacuum direction has the eigenvalues"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0d8ade6b-1eaa-4d8b-a8d0-b68fe1d7ff9f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[Lambda]", 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["amp",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
   RowBox[{"(", "\[Omega]", ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
   FractionBox[
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["G", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SH",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    RowBox[{"4", 
     SuperscriptBox["\[Pi]", "2"]}]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[Integral]", "0", "1"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["q", "TI"], "2"], 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["q", "TI"], "2"], "+", 
       SubsuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["LL",
         FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"]}], ")"}], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["dq", "TI"]}], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["E", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["E", "TI"], "2"], "-", 
       SuperscriptBox["\[Omega]", "2"], "/", "4"}], ")"}]}]], ","}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 FontFamily->"Times",
 FontSize->1.25 
  Inherited,ExpressionUUID->"e05074ae-b0f2-40fe-bbab-af429823e2a5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[Lambda]", 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["ph",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
   RowBox[{"(", "\[Omega]", ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
   FractionBox[
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["G", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SH",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    RowBox[{"4", 
     SuperscriptBox["\[Pi]", "2"]}]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[Integral]", "0", "1"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["q", "TI"], "2"], 
     StyleBox["E", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["dq", "TI"]}], 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["E", "TI"], "2"], "-", 
     SuperscriptBox["\[Omega]", "2"], "/", "4"}]], ","}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 FontFamily->"Times",
 FontSize->1.25 
  Inherited,ExpressionUUID->"6bd6471e-6e02-4909-93df-b47c173aff71"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["E", "TI"], "2"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["q", "TI"], "2"], "+", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "+", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["SH",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], "0"], ")"}], "2"], "/", "4"}], TraditionalForm]],
   "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4f69fee9-dfc4-4c42-8055-492483410b8c"],
 ", the forms of the theory of Bardeen, Cooper and Schrieffer; a mode lies \
where one of them equals 1. The phase eigenvalue at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[Omega]", "\[LongEqual]", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bb41cdf6-435e-4359-97d0-dacc7733b631"],
 " is the gap equation, so it equals 1 there: the Goldstone mode. The \
identity of the integrands, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["q", "TI"], "2"], "+", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["m", "TI"], "2"]}], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["E", "TI"], 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        SuperscriptBox[
         StyleBox["E", "TI"], "2"], "-", 
        SuperscriptBox["\[Omega]", "2"], "/", "4"}], ")"}]}]], "-", 
    FractionBox["1", 
     StyleBox["E", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox["\[Omega]", "2"], "-", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["d", "TI"], "2"]}], 
     RowBox[{"4", 
      StyleBox["E", "TI"], 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        SuperscriptBox[
         StyleBox["E", "TI"], "2"], "-", 
        SuperscriptBox["\[Omega]", "2"], "/", "4"}], ")"}]}]]}], 
   TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "26c439a3-3257-436c-9b39-93b0dc10c470"],
 ", gives"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"234b86b5-7c75-47d4-af07-1eae0b1e12dd"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[Lambda]", 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["amp",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
   RowBox[{"(", "\[Omega]", ")"}], "-", "1", "\[LongEqual]", 
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["\[Omega]", "2"], "-", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"(", 
       SubsuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["SH",
         FontSlant->"Plain"], "0"], ")"}], "2"]}], "4"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   FractionBox[
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["G", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SH",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    RowBox[{"4", 
     SuperscriptBox["\[Pi]", "2"]}]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[Integral]", "0", "1"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["q", "TI"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["dq", "TI"]}], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["E", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["E", "TI"], "2"], "-", 
       SuperscriptBox["\[Omega]", "2"], "/", "4"}], ")"}]}]], ","}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 FontFamily->"Times",
 FontSize->1.25 
  Inherited,ExpressionUUID->"45ae301c-23f6-42b6-bd1a-984f30075f45"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "and the integral is positive below the threshold ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"2", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SH",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["eff",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"4", 
       SubsuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["LL",
         FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "+", 
       SuperscriptBox[
        RowBox[{"(", 
         SubsuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["SH",
           FontSlant->"Plain"], "0"], ")"}], "2"]}], ")"}], 
     RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d34233de-e670-400b-82b3-b496b70d9930"],
 ", where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["E", "TI"], "2"], "-", 
    SuperscriptBox["\[Omega]", "2"], "/", "4", ">", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "80661686-2f30-4631-a4b7-8ef3d8bcaac9"],
 " for every momentum. So ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[Lambda]", 
     StyleBox["SH",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["amp",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", "1"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a0fa0408-bf61-4e21-9d27-4713c543ec4b"],
 " only at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[Omega]", "\[LongEqual]", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SH",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "0"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5ab8f3eb-acad-4eb4-8b7d-45ee915afe97"],
 ", for every coupling, mass and cutoff. The cell proves the identity and the \
positivity symbolically (the latter by deciding a statement about all real \
numbers), evaluates the integrals with 30 digits, finds the root of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[Lambda]", 
     StyleBox["SH",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["amp",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", "1"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c245dc00-bd5e-4e6d-b30c-74b70324c48a"],
 " and compares the frequencies that the Rust program found from the linear \
response of the whole sector, without the closed forms. The two closed forms \
themselves were found by comparison with the response of the Python program, \
not derived by hand. ",
 StyleBox["Why it matters.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " (1) It is the result of the theory of Bardeen, Cooper and Schrieffer, in \
which the amplitude mode lies at twice the gap parameter; here ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SH",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "0"], "/", "2"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9d5ad091-3f71-4bba-ac0e-5bef55dd65a7"],
 " plays that role, and the mass ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["LL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2c183137-352e-4855-805e-504643d04bde"],
 " raises the lowest quasi-particle energy to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["eff",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b4569c50-82d1-4c74-b8b3-61786126a3b9"],
 ", so that the mode is bound below the threshold, a sharp particle of the \
mean field. (2) It fixes the mass of the candidate for the Higgs boson: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["H",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "/", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["v", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SH",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SH",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "0"], "/", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["v", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SH",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "57d5cf52-55ca-48b2-a775-14beafd559b5"],
 ", about 8 in the second version against ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["H", "TI"]], "/", 
    StyleBox["v", "TI"], "\[TildeTilde]", "0.51"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2c37f5c1-7433-4110-8806-e1b756d01b01"],
 " in the Standard Model (check WH-4). (3) The effective Lagrangian fails \
here: it gives a frequency above the threshold, because an expansion in the \
frequency cannot hold for a mode so close to it. (4) The mode at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "0"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3d832e68-df9e-4934-aeee-14826e2a0a85"],
 " holds in the time domain too (Section R.4), and only in the pairing-only \
methods: with the scalar and the vector terms, HS (1, 1) puts it somewhat \
lower, still bound, and KS and CJT put it above the energy that breaks a \
pair, where it decays. (5) It is a mean-field result; the fluctuations beyond \
the mean field are not computed."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f071368f-8181-4d49-9c4c-34234c2f2160"],

