 InterpretationBox[
  RowBox[{"\<\"PASS \"\>", "\[InvisibleSpace]", "\<\"WH-5\"\>", 
   "\[InvisibleSpace]", "\<\"  \"\>", 
   "\[InvisibleSpace]", "\<\"HS (0, 0): the identity (k^2 + m^2) / (E (E^2 - \
w^2/4)) - 1/E = (w^2 - d^2) / (4 E (E^2 - w^2/4)) with E^2 = k^2 + m^2 + \
d^2/4 holds for every momentum (symbolic) and E^2 - w^2/4 > 0 for w < 2 M_eff \
(symbolic), so that lambda_amp(w) = 1 only at w = d_0; the continuum \
integrals give |lambda_amp(d_0) - 1| = 0 and |lambda_phase(0) - 1| = 0 (the \
gap equation), the root of lambda_amp = 1 is 0.81284554632043386736 against \
d_0 = 0.81284554632043386736, below 2 M_eff = 0.9059348112159973 (binding \
0.0930893); the amplitude modes of the Rust program (HS (0, 1) and HS (0, 0), \
both versions) equal d_0 (relative)\"\>", "\[InvisibleSpace]", "\<\" [\"\>", 
   "\[InvisibleSpace]", "\<\"identity True, positivity True; Rust deviation \
8.442e-13\"\>", "\[InvisibleSpace]", "\<\"]   [the same check: Rust \"\>", 
