rational offsets, exactly) and the value 1/2 at x = 1 (limit), so that the \
half width at half maximum of a pure cosine is 2 pi / T = 0.020943951 for the \
runs of length 300; the widths of the sampled cosines of the Rust program \
against it (relative)\"\>", "\[InvisibleSpace]", "\<\" [\"\>", 
   "\[InvisibleSpace]", "\<\"form True, half True, deviation 5.037e-7\"\>", 
   "\[InvisibleSpace]", "\<\"]   [the same check: Rust \"\>", 
   "\[InvisibleSpace]", "\<\"D-4b\"\>", 
   "\[InvisibleSpace]", "\<\", Python \"\>", 
   "\[InvisibleSpace]", "\<\"none\"\>", "\[InvisibleSpace]", "\<\"]\"\>"}],
  SequenceForm[
  "PASS ", "WD-4", "  ", 
   "the Hann window: its normalized transform has the modulus |sin(x pi) / (x \
pi (1 - x^2))| at the offset x 2 pi / T (the squared modulus of the exact \
integral equals that of the closed form at nine rational offsets, exactly) \
and the value 1/2 at x = 1 (limit), so that the half width at half maximum of \
a pure cosine is 2 pi / T = 0.020943951 for the runs of length 300; the \
widths of the sampled cosines of the Rust program against it (relative)", 
   " [", "form True, half True, deviation 5.037e-7", 
   "]   [the same check: Rust ", "D-4b", ", Python ", "none", "]"],
